PURPOSE

H134 showed that representation-debt markers can be compressed into fit-gated debt families while retaining high future recall and reducing storage.

H135 asks:

WHEN ONE DORMANT DEBT-FAMILY MEMBER BECOMES HIGH VALUE,

can shared family structure reduce the evidence cost of re-auditing related unresolved sites

WITHOUT

turning one local cue into broad false promotion?

BOUNDARY

This is synthetic research only.

It does not:
- implement biological tissue;
- establish a production architecture;
- freeze a representation metric;
- execute or modify STAB-18-R1;
- spend canonical scientific execution;
- authorize deployment or runtime activation.

EVIDENCE

SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

PREREGISTERED PRIMARY HYPOTHESIS

A fit-gated canary reactivation policy should outperform:
- isolated individual re-audition on evidence efficiency; and
- unconditional family broadcast on false-promotion control.

The mechanism is:

1. reactivate a small canary subset from the debt family;
2. measure fresh residual agreement under current context;
3. broadcast re-audition only if fresh canary agreement clears a fit gate;
4. otherwise remain local.

SYNTHETIC ECOLOGY

Primary confirmation:
2,000 worlds.

Each world contains:
- 8 to 14 latent debt families;
- one rarity-weighted reactivation target family;
- 18 to 70 dormant members in the target family;
- five-dimensional residual state;
- heterogeneous member value;
- two-dimensional local/context coordinates;
- fresh post-dormancy drift.

Regimes:

R1 — FAMILY-STABLE
The family remains coherent.

R2 — SINGLE-MEMBER-DRIFT
A very small local subset diverges.

R3 — SUBGROUP-DRIFT
A coherent minority local subgroup diverges.

R4 — WHOLE-FAMILY-SHIFT
Most members move together into a new residual regime.

The target family is rarity-weighted so current frequency is not treated as future option value.

COMPARATORS

A — INDIVIDUAL
Audit only the triggering member.

B — BLIND BROADCAST
Audit the trigger, then use it as family-wide evidence with no fresh family-fit gate.

C — FIXED CANARY
Audit a small non-adaptive canary set.
Broadcast when agreement clears the primary agreement threshold.

D — FIT-GATED ADAPTIVE CANARY
Audit the trigger plus a small spatially diverse canary set.
Estimate a robust fresh family center.
Broadcast only when:
agreement >= 0.80
AND
normalized dispersion <= 0.65.

E — FULL FAMILY CHECK
Audit every member.
This is the expensive evidence-quality upper bound.

PRIMARY COST / VALUE SCALE

Correctly resolved member benefit:
3.0 x member value.

Incorrect promotion cost:
5.0 x member value.

Evidence audit cost:
1.0 per audited member.

Broadcast application cost:
0.20 per reached member.

Dormant unresolved carry cost:
0.15 x member value.

The scale is synthetic and only supports policy comparison inside this toy ecology.

