16.01 percentage points.

Thus the positive result is not dependent on one exact threshold or one exact canary fraction.

FIXED-CANARY COMPARISON

The adaptive policy did not dominate the fixed canary comparator everywhere.

Across the 81 robustness combinations:
adaptive net > fixed-canary net in:
38.27%.

Median fixed-minus-adaptive net:
0.64 value units.

Interpretation:

Under benign stable or nearly coherent families,
non-adaptive canaries can be slightly cheaper in opportunity terms because they broadcast more readily.

Under subgroup drift,
diverse adaptive canaries improve containment.

Primary subgroup-drift mean net:

adaptive:
12.03 to 12.26 in repeated stress/primary samples.

fixed:
8.76 in primary confirmation.

The correct conclusion is not:

ADAPTIVE CANARIES ALWAYS WIN.

The supported conclusion is:

FRESH FIT GATING IS NECESSARY,
AND
CANARY TOPOLOGY MATTERS MOST WHEN THE FAMILY IS INTERNALLY HETEROGENEOUS.

