PRIMARY TOPOLOGY LIMIT

Locally clustered canaries often agree with one another
while failing to represent the rest of the family.

That produces:

HIGH APPARENT CONFIDENCE
+
LOW REPRESENTATIVENESS
=
FALSE BROADCAST.

This is a distinct failure mode from ordinary residual noise.

Therefore:

CANARY AGREEMENT
IS NOT SUFFICIENT.

The organism also needs:

CANARY COVERAGE / REPRESENTATIVENESS.

HIGH-VALUE CONTRADICTOR STRESS

A targeted stress forced one high-value member to contradict an otherwise coherent family and made that contradictory member the trigger.

